## **Summary**

**Key Rules:**
1. **Never use iframe** - Givebutter blocks iframe embedding with X-Frame-Options
2. **Use popup window on desktop** - `window.open()` works around X-Frame-Options restrictions
3. **Use new tab on mobile** - Mobile browsers handle popups poorly; new tab ensures PRB works
4. **Wait for script** - Always check if Givebutter script is loaded before using custom elements
5. **Provide fallbacks** - Multiple fallback strategies ensure reliability
6. **Handle popup blocking** - Gracefully fallback to new tab if popup is blocked
7. **Monitor popup closure** - Use intervals to detect when popup closes (for analytics)
8. **Detect mobile devices** - Use user agent and screen width to determine mobile vs desktop

**Implementation Checklist:**
- [ ] Givebutter script added to root layout with `strategy="afterInteractive"`
- [ ] TypeScript declarations file created for custom elements
- [ ] Donate button component uses popup window (desktop) or new tab (mobile)
- [ ] Mobile device detection implemented (user agent + screen width)
- [ ] Script loading detection implemented with polling
- [ ] Fallback to new tab if popup is blocked
- [ ] Popup dimensions set to 800x900px and centered (desktop only)
- [ ] Cleanup for timers/intervals implemented
- [ ] Error handling and logging included

**Mobile PRB Support:**
- ✅ **Apple Pay**: Automatically supported when Givebutter page opens in new tab on iOS Safari
- ✅ **Google Pay**: Automatically supported when Givebutter page opens in new tab on Chrome/Android
- ✅ **No Additional Configuration**: Givebutter handles PRB display automatically based on device capabilities
- ✅ **HTTPS Required**: Ensure your site uses HTTPS (required for Apple Pay)

**Cover image & description (optional, not implemented):**
- **Modal (current):** Checkout only; no cover/description. Keep popup/modal as default.
- **Full campaign page (optional):** Cover + description shown. See **Optional: Cover Image & Description (Future Integration)** above if we want to switch to always opening the full campaign page (popup/tab) later.

This ensures reliable Givebutter donation widget integration that works across all browsers and devices while respecting security restrictions and enabling mobile payment methods (Apple Pay/Google Pay PRB).
